{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "A Gothic window",
  "description": "A Gothic window: two small pointed arches from the first three circles, a big arch over both from two circles twice the size, a mullion up the middle of each small arch, and a round window where two more circles cross, just touching every arch. The small arches blue, the round window red, the rest of the big arch purple.",
  "steps": [
    "A circle centered on 0, through 1.",
    "A circle centered on 1, through 0. Where they cross is the point of the first small arch.",
    "A line through 0 and 1. It reaches a new point at 2.",
    "A circle centered on 2, through 1. That makes the second small arch.",
    "A big circle centered on 0, through 2.",
    "A big circle centered on 2, through 0. Where they cross is the point of the big arch.",
    "A line through the crossings of the first two circles. It marks the middle of the first small arch.",
    "The same for the second small arch.",
    "A circle centered on 0, through the middle of the second small arch.",
    "A circle centered on 2, through the middle of the first. These two cross where the round window will be centered.",
    "A line from 0 through that center. It crosses the first circle just below it.",
    "The round window: centered there, through that crossing. It just touches every arch around it."
  ],
